From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Markus Volk <f_l_k@t-online.de>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 11:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] QtCore: drop QEvent::EnterEditFocus and LeaveEditFocus

Qt 6.12 removed both enumerators along with keypad navigation, but PyQt6 still
exposes them unconditionally, so the generated bindings do not compile:

  sipQtCoreQEvent.cpp:624:57: error: 'EnterEditFocus' is not a member of 'QEvent'
  sipQtCoreQEvent.cpp:625:57: error: 'LeaveEditFocus' is not a member of 'QEvent'

The %Timeline in sip/QtCore/QtCoremod.sip ends at Qt_6_11_0, so there is no
version tag to guard them with; drop them instead.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 sip/QtCore/qcoreevent.sip | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sip/QtCore/qcoreevent.sip b/sip/QtCore/qcoreevent.sip
--- a/sip/QtCore/qcoreevent.sip
+++ b/sip/QtCore/qcoreevent.sip
@@ -200,8 +200,6 @@
         PlatformSurface,
         TabletTrackingChange,
         GraphicsSceneLeave,
-        EnterEditFocus,
-        LeaveEditFocus,
 %If (Qt_6_6_0 -)
         DevicePixelRatioChange,
 %End
